== 3b. every refusal message, sorted, so the expected output reads them ==
  latte$entry.BadCatchAll: route "/files/{*rest}": a catch-all placeholder ("{*rest}") is not supported — a placeholder captures one segment
  latte$entry.BadClashB and latte$entry.BadClashA both answer GET /clash/{}; nothing at request time could choose between them
  latte$entry.BadClashB and latte$entry.BadClashA both answer GET /clash/{}; nothing at request time could choose between them
  latte$entry.BadDuplicatePlaceholder: route "/dup/{a}/{a}" names "a" twice
  latte$entry.BadLayoutAmbiguous: @layout(name: "Attr") is ambiguous — latte.Attr, latte$entry.Attr; spell the qualified name
  latte$entry.BadLayoutLoop: the layout chain loops at latte$entry.LoopA
  latte$entry.BadLayoutNotALayout: @layout(name: "Counter") resolves to latte$entry.Counter, which does not extend latte.Layout
  latte$entry.BadLayoutUnknown: @layout(name: "Nope") names no type in this program
  latte$entry.BadNoMethods: @page(methods:) is empty
  latte$entry.BadOrphanPlaceholder: route "/orphan/{missing}" captures "missing" but no @param binds it
  latte$entry.BadPlaceholder: route "/x/o{id}": a placeholder is a whole segment, so "o{id}" is not one
  latte$entry.BadPrivateParam.secret is a @param but is not public, and reflection does not bypass visibility
  latte$entry.BadRequiredNotInRoute.id is @param(required: true) but route "/needs-nothing" does not capture "id"
  latte$entry.BadRouteStart: a route must start with "/"; this one is "counter"
  latte$entry.BadUnbindable.tags is captured by route "/unbindable/{tags}" but is a List<string>; a route can bind string, int, bool and float
  latte$entry.NotAComponent is annotated @page but does not extend latte.Component, so it has nothing to render
  latte$entry.NotAPageButGuarded is annotated @authorize but is not a @page; the requirement would never be checked
  latte$entry.NotAPageButWrapped is annotated @layout but is neither a @page nor a latte.Layout, so nothing would ever wrap it

